                <pb facs="0980" n="856" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg856"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.522/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-04T18:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 4, 1923—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 4—1:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>64. My 62, July 3, 5 p.m. After further consideration we have decided it would be
                    preferable to withhold temporarily proposal of <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi> in order that we may urge element of time as reason for
                    proceeding at once with negotiations. If at the promised conference we find [it]
                    impracticable to proceed with negotiations, proposal will be maintained for <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
